<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Merged into the generated macOS Info.plist by Tauri at bundle time.
	  NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription is required on modern macOS for the app to
	  connect to an OpenAI-/Anthropic-compatible model server on the local
	  network (e.g. http://192.168.x.x:1234/v1). Without it the connection is
	  denied with no prompt. The string is shown verbatim in the permission
	  dialog, so it is bilingual (Japanese, then English).
	-->
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>WAKARU は、ローカルネットワーク上の AI モデルサーバー（OpenAI 互換・Anthropic 互換エンドポイント）へ接続するためにローカルネットワークへのアクセスを使用します。 — WAKARU uses local network access to reach AI model servers on your network (OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible endpoints).</string>
</dict>
</plist>
